atlas commands-hypervisor-owner

architecture hypervisor-bun-compilation-owner
  canonical_name HypervisorBunCompilationOwner
  family commands
  domain Execution / Governed mission compilation and provider registry
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can the installed mission semantics become a shared content-addressed plan without confusing provider reachability, compilation and authorization to execute?
  purpose Retire Python registry and mission compilation into bounded Bun owners and share planning identity with V6 and Recursive representations.
  internal_calculus trait descriptors -> exact mission task DAG -> content-addressed input identities -> durable specification and candidate execution plan
  internal_calculus all requested capabilities -> one indexed route query -> ordered eligible candidates -> selected-provider input identity -> downstream invalidation
  internal_calculus bounded concurrent native probes -> ordered secret-safe observations -> one registry update transaction
  invariant compilation retains the original R7 task and authority distinctions; task execution and canary success are not inferred
  invariant historical receipts preserve Python default-space canonicalization and raw numeric identities without rewriting source evidence
  invariant process admission is shared with V6; Python and unknown shell trampolines cannot silently re-enter retired paths
  invariant candidate reuse requires verified output identity, current authority, current input residency and effect-specific replay policy
  forbidden_inference content identity, a compiled mission or fewer SQL statements -> valid cached effects, semantic provider capability or distributed throughput
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_schema.sql
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_store.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_missions.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_discovery.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/native_probe.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_hypervisor_bridge.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_server.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_catalog.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_catalog.json
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_cli.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_adapters.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_evaluation.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_sources.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_store.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_missions.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_discovery.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_hypervisor_bridge.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_transport.test.mjs default server path compiles all ten mission templates into candidate state
  witness tests/hypervisor_history_witness.json verifies all nineteen historical receipts on a disposable copy with source bytes unchanged
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_route_benchmark.json source-bound copied-registry comparison with equal route results and twelve-to-one statement reduction
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_discovery_benchmark.json seven alternating paired scans with real child processes and controlled synthetic latency; no production speed claim
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_analysis.json Oxlint 1.86.0, twenty-two source-bound files, ninety-six rules and zero diagnostics
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_server.test.mjs all thirty-three tools retain dispatch contracts; default composition compiles and persists real context without injected engines; cold STOP reads do not initialize a database
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_cli.test.mjs native task-execute and schema-driven argument parsing
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_adapters.test.mjs reviewed executable boundaries, bounded children and no arbitrary compact-command shell
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_evaluation.test.mjs capability-specific behavior, current certificates and actual SQLite persistence; reachability never grants semantic success
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_sources.test.mjs disposable local Git fixtures verify source identity, update candidates and failed acquisition without retry
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_runtime_analysis.json actual Oxlint 1.86.0 checks thirty-six source-bound files with ninety-six rules and no diagnostics
  known_gap the thirty-three-operation Bun service is source-implemented and fixture-verified, not live-promoted; the installed Python daemon remains running
  known_gap Bernstein is still an explicitly named upstream Python CLI; unsandboxed acquired source tests refuse; neither boundary counts as Python retirement
  known_gap default external effects require an independent authority owner and mission goal verification requires an independent typed verifier; neither permission nor verdict is synthesized
  known_gap filesystem artifacts and SQLite state are not one atomic transaction; interrupted compilation leaves explicit reconciliation receipts

architecture hypervisor-context-body-cut
  canonical_name HypervisorContextBodyCut
  family representation
  domain Representation / Purpose-bound mission context residency
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can concurrent missions share exact source bodies without sharing authorization or silently changing mandatory instructions?
  internal_calculus exact UTF-8 source body -> SHA-256 address -> required inline or explicit optional reference -> purpose-bound rendered body -> durable packet receipt
  internal_calculus full rendered envelope -> declared tokenizer counter or explicitly approximate byte estimate -> bounded cut or refusal
  invariant goal, mission constraints, task definitions and explicit evidence remain intact or compilation refuses; there is no prose substitution or silent truncation
  invariant equal body identity permits byte residency sharing only; each packet retains its own purpose, task plan and receipt
  invariant every render rechecks owned packet bytes and referenced source body digests
  forbidden_inference shared context bytes or byte estimates -> shared policy, native model token counts, admissible external evidence or authority to execute
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_context.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_store.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_context.test.mjs exact reuse, purpose separation, full-envelope accounting, body tamper, STOP and cancellation
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_context_benchmark.json twelve real disposable compiles with exact synthetic-body equality and measured byte residency; no production latency or token-saving claim
  known_gap the default mission context has no native model-tokenizer binding; budget_verified is false and exact counts are null until a declared counter is bound
  known_gap this context does not bypass AddressPlane/ForeignTwin admission and is not a substitute for the separately governed ContextCut material frontier

architecture hypervisor-durable-task-execution
  canonical_name HypervisorDurableTaskExecution
  family execution
  domain Execution / Bounded owner orchestration and effect reconciliation
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question How can a semantic task DAG advance concurrently without stale policy, stale provider eligibility or crash recovery silently replaying an effect?
  internal_calculus immutable task plan -> cached task indexes -> bounded ready waves -> indexed dependency reads -> atomic revision and provider eligibility check -> FULL SQLite intent commit -> exact owner call -> bound outcome
  internal_calculus task input plus packet plus route plus provider plus non-downgradable effect class -> domain-separated attempt identity
  invariant an interrupted attempt is not retried; uncertain effects require reconciliation and running siblings are joined before the execution scope ends
  invariant mission revisions advance monotonically on semantic or routing updates; stale dispatch, completion and finalization refuse
  invariant accepted work and two completed agent runs do not prove a mission goal; resolved requires an independent typed behavioral-verification receipt
  forbidden_inference matching input identity, successful transport or completed agent work -> permission, exactly-once external execution or verified mission success
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_execution.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/hypervisor_store.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_execution.test.mjs bounded parallel waves, sibling joining, real context/store integration, uncertainty, separate goal verdict and concurrent provider quarantine
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_store.test.mjs restarted intent refusal, exact attempt completion, revision invalidation and event byte bounds
  witness 2026-10-03 live owners, mission 45095ca358914685806965f777458cb8: substrate.mission.bootstrap failed (receipt 97fe897be66d490ab53a7dadefcd1e43) although the recursive owner returned a passing receipt and all seven IR projections each with a digest; acceptance had required a bundle-level ir_bundle.digest the owner never emits
  witness 2026-10-03 live owners, mission fdf68c9dcc7e47f88ddc9d1b6ebb827b: with acceptance changed to require the seven projections, T-001, T-001A, T-001B, T-001C and T-002 passed; one run, no fixture
  forbidden_inference seven IR projections each carrying a digest -> a bundle-level content identity; none is computed or compared
  known_gap the seven-projection bootstrap acceptance has no fixture test; it is witnessed by one live run only
  known_gap fabric tasks dispatch only when the selected provider is bonfyre-native, while live routing selects claude-code for agent.architect; an authorized T-003 blocked as native fabric owner unavailable, so no live mission has advanced past the first agent task
  known_gap each owner process consults the operator STOP file itself; a stop override at the hypervisor does not reach them, and the spines owner returned the temporal bootstrap as uncertain while STOP was present
  known_gap remote owner authorization remains at each exact owner; this ledger is not a distributed transaction and cannot prove exactly-once external effects
  known_gap local fixtures do not establish distributed throughput or production deployment

interaction hypervisor-default-context-cut
  source hypervisor-bun-compilation-owner
  destination hypervisor-context-body-cut
  relation default-owned-context-compilation
  preserves purpose, exact source identities, semantic task plan, mandatory evidence and explicit absence
  drops mutable per-mission section files and lossy prose rewriting
  forbidden_inference content-addressed context -> admitted evidence or provider authority
  binding integrations/mcp/hypervisor_server.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_server.test.mjs

interaction hypervisor-executes-shared-task-plan
  source hypervisor-durable-task-execution
  destination semantic-task-input-plan
  relation bounded-ready-wave-execution
  preserves exact dependencies and recomputed plan identity with current context, route, provider and effect binding
  drops per-task full-mission scans and generic verified-boolean success
  forbidden_inference deterministic DAG -> deterministic remote effects or mission goal proof
  binding integrations/mcp/hypervisor_execution.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_execution.test.mjs

interaction hypervisor-execution-consumes-context-body-cut
  source hypervisor-durable-task-execution
  destination hypervisor-context-body-cut
  relation exact-purpose-bound-owner-input
  preserves rendered body bytes and current packet digest in task attempt identity
  drops sending a local packet pathname as if it were model context
  forbidden_inference native packet rendering -> model tokenizer compatibility or remote residency
  binding integrations/mcp/hypervisor_execution.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_execution.test.mjs

architecture semantic-task-input-plan
  canonical_name SemanticTaskInputPlan
  family execution
  domain Execution / Incremental semantic planning
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Which task inputs changed and which exact downstream computations must be reconsidered without rebuilding semantic authority?
  internal_calculus canonical task definition plus mission-wide policy context plus parent input identities -> transitive task input digest
  internal_calculus immutable validated DAG -> indexed downstream cut -> candidate invalidation; global policy change invalidates every candidate
  invariant duplicate tasks, dangling dependencies and cycles refuse before durable compilation
  invariant mutable execution status is not part of semantic input identity; selected provider and task acceptance contracts are
  invariant serialized plan descriptors are not trusted indexes; representation owners recompute identity from semantic inputs
  forbidden_inference unchanged input digest -> authorized output reuse or permission to skip an effect
  source_path integrations/mcp/mission_plan.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/mission_plan.test.mjs exact two-node one-edge invalidation in a ten-thousand-task forest
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_store.test.mjs all seven IRs bind the shared recomputed plan identity
  known_gap this is candidate work selection, not a complete result cache, distributed scheduler or incremental compiler that avoids every whole-plan scan

interaction hypervisor-compiles-semantic-input-plan
  source hypervisor-bun-compilation-owner
  destination semantic-task-input-plan
  relation default-mission-compilation
  preserves task dependencies, provider selection, constraints and mission policy
  drops repeated ad hoc graph identity and unbound cache decisions
  forbidden_inference plan identity -> execution authority
  binding integrations/mcp/hypervisor_missions.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/hypervisor_missions.test.mjs

interaction recursive-ir-binds-task-plan
  source recursive-substrate-native-owner
  destination semantic-task-input-plan
  relation representation-shared-input-identity
  preserves one recomputed task-plan digest across all seven IRs and per-task roots in DeltaIR
  drops trust in caller-supplied execution-plan metadata
  forbidden_inference representation agreement -> deployment, successful execution or authority
  binding integrations/mcp/recursive_store.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_store.test.mjs

